                <pb facs="0406" n="306" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/2716: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Jefferson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-11T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 11,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>47. Department has received reports of protests by Coalitionists in Bluefields
                    against alleged action of Government in preventing voters from voting and to the
                    effect that Coalitionists have cast their votes in the presence of notaries.
                    Endeavor to get full report from Consul and transmit to Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
